  claudebox agent enrol      open another enrolment window, for one more machine
  claudebox agent status     whether that front door is up, and its fingerprint
  claudebox agent add <host:port> <code>
                             the other side of it, run ON a runner machine
  claudebox agent show|test|forget

  claudebox mutagen start    share this machine's workspace, so another machine
                             on the LAN can keep a live local copy of the same
                             source tree and run its own claudebox against it.
                             Prints the address and the host key to compare.
  claudebox mutagen stop     stop sharing it (the host key and the authorised
                             keys are kept)
  claudebox mutagen status   whether it is up, which machines may log in, and --
                             on a machine that has attached -- whether the copy
                             is actually current
  claudebox mutagen authorize '<public key>'
                             let a machine in, using the line its "attach"
                             printed. Keys only -- there is no password.

